WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.410
South Sudan became
independent on 9 July 2011.

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:10.650
On 15 December 2013, violence broke out
in Juba and spread across the country.

3
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:16.110
Almost 500,000 people were displaced
within the country in the first month.

4
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.390
Tens of thousands of civilians
fled to UN compounds in Juba,

5
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.570
Bor, Akobo, Bentiu, Malakal and Melut.

6
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:28.170
Years later, who protects
and supports them today?

7
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.130
In this mission, you'll see how
governance works at different scales,

8
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.910
from the UN to a national
government to NGOs.

9
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.050
Then you'll weigh the consequences
for local communities in the camps.

10
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.810
Your mission: find out who protects and
supports South Sudan's displaced people

11
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.560
today.
